Well, okay so let's separate emotional experiences

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.843
and defenses from physiological chemical events.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:59.180
So, on a chemical level, take a substance like cocaine

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.580
or crystal meth or nicotine or caffeine,

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:03.380
these are stimulants.

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.460
They elevate the level of a chemical in the brain

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:08.150
which we referred to already called dopamine.

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:12.640
And dopamine is the incentive vitality excitement molecule.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:17.640
Without that, we're listless bored, a motivated,

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.623
disinterested, you nerd.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:25.750
So the dopamine circuitry is crucial to human life

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:26.963
and human motivation.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:30.670
But the development of the dopamine circuitry depends

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:33.300
on the presence of a nurturing parent.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.630
So if you dig into the monkeys

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:38.110
and they measure the dopamine level one week

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:40.350
after separation from the mother,

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:42.823
the dopamine levels are significantly diminished.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:49.020
And dopamine receptors are diminished

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:52.020
when there's a lot of stress around.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:54.680
Or you can isolate the monkeys or rats and put them into

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.770
an isolation cage and then measure the dopamine receptors

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:59.820
a month later, it's significantly diminished.

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:02.420
So the brain is responsive to the environment

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.520
and especially in early childhood.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.133
So there's the chemical effects.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:08.640
